  "body": "From the OpenClaw comms design for #2023 (doc PR for task 3381), gap G2/G4.\n\nThe OpenClaw gateway binds the laptop tailnet address (100.99.113.103:18789, verified by `ss`) while `gateway.auth.token` is a secret reference the CLI path cannot resolve and status reports loopback auth \"none\". The socket bind — not the \"Tailscale exposure: off\" status flag — is authoritative for reachability, so the tailnet bind is real exposure and must require authentication.\n\nWork:\n- Determine/enforce token authentication for non-loopback gateway callers; per-caller identity for consumers (Muse's gateway client is the first).\n- Provision/rotate the token through the existing secrets manager, referenced by name only — never written into config files, docs, or chat.\n- If the gateway cannot enforce auth on the tailnet bind specifically, restrict the bind to loopback until it can, and record that outcome on #2023.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [ ] A non-loopback gateway request without a valid token is rejected, demonstrated live.\n- [ ] The enforcement/provisioning outcome is recorded on #2023 and in the design doc's follow-up state.\n- [ ] No credential value appears in any repo file, issue, or log.\n",
